member.summary:
            The font a letter of words is drawn from beside a big font that is read, and its number there, as AutoCAD 2021 draws
            it (check F3), and how many letters it takes; the font null for a letter neither has, and false where it is not
            measured. The letter is read as bytes in the big font's code page (ASCII as itself), and drawn:


°, ± and ∅, the signs of %%d, %%p and %%c, from the font where it has them;

a byte that opens a letter of two in the big font, with the next letter's byte, as that letter of the big font
            (special.shx's "~!");

a space as the big font's where it has one (extfont.shx's, 9 of 15 wide), else the font's;

another byte alone as the font's letter, else the big font's;

a letter of two bytes as the big font's (中, Ж beside extfont.shx), else the font's (Ж beside gbcbig.shx), and
            the ideographic space a space;

a letter the page has not as the font's.

            Not measured: a letter beyond ASCII beside a big font of no code page or a font of shapes, and a byte that opens a
            letter of two before one of two bytes.

Lines, arcs and polylines of the plane of a LWPOLYLINE or a POLYLINE of the plane end to end into it: each a run of
vertices in the system of its normal at its elevation, the arc of a piece whose normal is the other way turned over;
the polyline closed where the chain comes back to its start.

Where along the line its  is measured from: its first ink, or the start of the line where it
starts with a space or is of spaces alone, ink left of the start not counted of a TrueType font or beside a big font;
romans "A" 4 high from 0.190, where AutoCAD 2021 puts the ink of a line of an MTEXT at its left edge.

member.remarks:
Each class marks its own method, so no list is shared between the classes:
[DxfType("LINE")] internal static DxfEntity Create(DxfItem item) => new DxfLine(item);
A record of a type no method makes an object of, or whose methods all give null, is a .

member.summary:
Puts the values of the table's TABLECONTENT in the form of R2007 and later (the opposite of
), and takes the part of the round trip that holds the cells of the form before it (its data
table, with what it owns) out. False where a value is of a kind that is not known: a text and a number are.

The groups of the 30 properties R2013 added to a style, from the round trip record AutoCAD 2021 keeps for them under the
style's extension dictionary of R2010 and before (RTVSPost2010Prop28 to 57, each with how it is set);
null where the style has none or it is not whole.

The angle a segment of a leader of a multileader style is kept to, as AutoCAD's AngleConstraint numbers it: a
step of 15 degrees, which the style holds in radians (groups 40 and 41 of an MLEADERSTYLE, 0.785398 for 45 degrees);
 where it gives none.

Gives an INSERT of an annotative block that holds no context the scale as its one context, the default, and its record
and that context the factors it has divided by the scale, as AutoCAD 2021 gave an INSERT the scale 1:50 (50 for 1);
its attributes get a context of the scale as well, and are not moved otherwise.

Gets the anonymous block that stands for the dynamic block the INSERT places, as AutoCAD's
AnonymousBlockTableRecord: its own block where that is such a copy, *U7 of the dynamic block BOLT;
null where it places the dynamic block itself, or no dynamic block.

The chain or loop of a polyline of the kind a typed conversion asks for, as  gives
it: a loop where  is set, else a chain, and with arcs where  is set;
refused where it has arcs and a straight kind is asked for, or a loop is asked for and it is none.

Gets or sets the justification of the text, as AutoCAD's Justify: its  and
 taken together, a text centred on its middle ;
 where the record gives neither.

The text of the first group of a code in the part of the record a text's groups are in: the type's own part of a TEXT;
of an ATTRIB or ATTDEF, its AcDbText part for a text's code and the part after it for an attribute's (2, 3, 70, 73,
74 and 280), as ezdxf reads them; the whole record in a file of R12. Null where it has none.

Gives an MTEXT the field of the dimension's text, as AutoCAD's FieldToMText: a copy of the dimension's field of
its words and its children, every group of them kept, given to the MTEXT's words in the place of the field it had;
where the dimension has none, the MTEXT's is taken out. The MTEXT's  are not changed.

Gets or sets the direction AutoCAD takes as level for the dimension (group 51, in degrees), as AutoCAD's
HorizontalRotation: in radians, the negative of the angle from the x of the normal's system to that of the user's;
nought where the record gives none.

Refuses a text style (group 7, as written) the text style table of a drawing an entity is added to does not list,
unless the entity is a copy of another drawing () that has it, which is copied with it;
nothing for no style or no drawing.

The lines of a table's grid, as AutoCAD's GridLineType flags them: of a cell, of a block of cells or of the rows
of a kind, the top and bottom lines, the left and right ones, and those inside between their rows and their columns;
 is the four round them, 45.

The own groups of the HATCH in parts, as ezdxf reads them: the loops from the first 91 on, as long as their codes run;
after them the gradient from its 450 to the end, the pattern's lines from its 78 as long as theirs run, and the seed
points from the 98; every other group a part of its own, in its place.

The edge as the lines of a pattern cut it, in the plane of the HATCH, from its start to its end as it runs: a line;
an arc or an ellipse as its centre and the two axes it turns between, over the parameters it runs over; a spline as
itself.

Gets the shape of a loop of a polyline, as AutoCAD's Polyline: a  for a closed one;
a  for one that is open, or so thin it closes no area the library takes, its first vertex
again at its end where it is closed. Null for a loop of edges.

Gets or sets what the leaders point to (group 172), as AutoCAD's ContentType;
 where the record gives none, and for a new MULTILEADER, which holds no words
yet ( false), as AutoCAD 2021 reads a new one (check D38b).

Gets the value of an attribute of the block, as AutoCAD's GetBlockAttribute: an ATTRIB in no file of the tag of
the attribute's definition and the value the MULTILEADER gives it (group 302 after the 330 of the definition's handle);
the definition's own value where the MULTILEADER gives none.

member.exception:
Thrown when the multileader has no context data, which AutoCAD draws it from;
            or is a copy in no file whose content or arrows are a block the drawing it was copied from has erased since, the
            handle of the block said.

member.summary:
Whether the content is moved with its landings, as AutoCAD 2021 moves it: words met on their sides (271 of nought),
running along the plane's x axis (13) or against it, as words mirrored across their plane run (check D38), or a block;
and the MULTILEADER is not being set from its style.

Gets whether the spline is periodic, as AutoCAD's Periodic: of a SPLINE, the flag 2 of its group 70, the periodic
of the DXF reference, which AutoCAD writes on its closed splines of a smooth seam too; 
is AutoCAD's reading, the flag 2048.

Sets the clip boundary, as AutoCAD's SetClipBoundary, and switches the clip on: two corners are a rectangle,
written as AutoCAD 2021 writes it, the upper left and the lower right, so that (1, 1) and (2, 2) are (1, 2) and (2, 1);
three or more are a polygon, written as given. The page's inches from its lower left corner, before the scale.

The vertices drawn in the editing's model (those of a fitted polyline's frame left out, as the reader leaves them):
points in the system of the normal at the elevation, bulges, widths (the default widths where a vertex gives none);
and the index of each one's record.

Writes a cell's override and its flag, its flags in a group of 91 from R2007 on, of 177 before, where it gives none;
nothing where the override the cell has of its own (its text, null for none) is the one given, which is checked
before it is written.

Gets the value a block cell gives an attribute of its block, as AutoCAD's GetBlockAttributeValue: the 300 after
the 331 that points at the definition, its escapes read as letters as  reads them;
null where the cell gives it none.

The text of the last group of a code after the table's last cell, where the library writes the table's own overrides;
where there is none there, the last of its head after its flags (93 to 96) and before its heights, where AutoCAD 2021
writes them: its flow (70) of a table it mirrored, its margins (40, 41), its title and header left out (280, 281).

Gives an edge of a cell the properties given (its colour, lineweight, showing; null for one not given), each its own
override with its flag where it differs, and the edge in the cell's edge flags (172), where they do not name it;
the cell copied apart into the edit where it changes. Whether it changed.

The scale that fits a block's extents, turned, into a cell less its margins, as AutoCAD fits a block cell: the least of
the cell's width less its two margins over the box's width and its height less its two over the box's height;
null where the box has no size or the cell holds none within its margins.

Gets the view along an axis the viewport shows, as AutoCAD's ViewOrthographic: 
where  is (0, 0, 1) to , and the five others likewise;
 for any other direction.

Gets the blocks the file defines, in the order of the file, each with its own entities in its own coordinates;
the INSERTs of the drawing are read in  as the entities they place. The blocks of the
layouts, *Model_Space and *Paper_Space, are not among them.

Gets the name of the linetype of the entity (group 6), such as DASHED, Continuous or ByBlock;
null where it takes the linetype of its layer, BYLAYER, written or not. An entity of a block whose linetype is
BYBLOCK has the linetype of the INSERT that placed it.

Adds a chain with arcs in space as it is: one lightweight polyline in its plane where it lies in one, and a LINE or
an ARC for each edge where it does not. The plane is judged at the global tolerance;
 states it.

member.remarks:
A box 30 by 20 by 10 is 12 triangles, wound outwards, whose signed volumes add up to 6 000. PostGIS reads the form;
it is the only well-known text for a body. Openings are cut in, and the triangles are made at the global tolerance.
A body the openings take all of is POLYHEDRALSURFACE Z EMPTY.

member.example:
On the console of a console application:

GeometryHelperLog.Writer = (level, message, exception) =>
    Console.WriteLine(GeometryHelperLog.Format(level, message, exception));

GeometryHelperLog.Info("Started.");   // prints: INFO Started.

On the status bar of Tekla Structures (using Tekla.Structures.Model.Operations; and
using GeometryHelper.Enums;). The bar shows one line at a time, the last one written,
so Debug detail is left out and the summary each conversion ends with stays on the bar:

GeometryHelperLog.Writer = (level, message, exception) =>
{
    if (level >= GeometryHelperLogLevel.Info)
    {
        Operation.DisplayPrompt(GeometryHelperLog.Format(level, message, exception));
    }
};

Every message in a file:

GeometryHelperLog.Writer = (level, message, exception) =>
    File.AppendAllText(logPath, GeometryHelperLog.Format(level, message, exception) + Environment.NewLine);

member.remarks:
The face is read by its material. Over the square 100 by 100 in the floor with a corner at the origin and a hole
40 by 40 in its middle, the segment from (45, 50, -10) to (45, 50, 10), through the hole, is 15 from the rim;
the segment from (20, 20, -10) to (20, 20, 10) crosses the material and is nought from it.

The face is read by its material. Over the square 100 by 100 in the floor with a corner at the origin and a hole
40 by 40 in its middle, the segment from (45, 50, -10) to (45, 50, 10), through the hole, is 15 from the rim;
the segment from (20, 20, -10) to (20, 20, 10) crosses the material and is nought from it.

The face is read by its material. Over the square 100 by 100 in the floor with a corner at the origin and a hole
40 by 40 in its middle, the ray from (45, 50, 10) pointing straight down, through the hole, is 15 from the rim;
from (20, 20, 10) it runs into the material and is nought from it.

The face is read by its material. Over the square 100 by 100 in the floor with a corner at the origin and a hole
40 by 40 in its middle, the ray from (45, 50, 10) pointing straight down, through the hole, is 15 from the rim;
from (20, 20, 10) it runs into the material and is nought from it.

The face is read by its material. Over the square 100 by 100 in the floor with a corner at the origin and a hole
40 by 40 in its middle, the segment from (45, 50, -10) to (45, 50, 10), through the hole, is 15 from the rim;
the segment from (20, 20, -10) to (20, 20, 10) crosses the material and is nought from it.

The face is read by its material. Over the square 100 by 100 in the floor with a corner at the origin and a hole
40 by 40 in its middle, the segment from (45, 50, -10) to (45, 50, 10), through the hole, is 15 from the rim;
the segment from (20, 20, -10) to (20, 20, 10) crosses the material and is nought from it.

