member.summary:
The place an earlier walk of this scanline stopped, for a bound at a greater X than its own, the nearest kept
below this X, or the last edge of the list kept that stands below this X, whichever stands at the greater X;
null where none is, and the walk starts at the head.

Sets the winding counts of a new edge of a closed path from the edges to its left. windCount, the count of
its own kind on the side of the edge where it is higher, follows from the nearest edge of the same kind;
windCount2, the count of the other kind, from the edges of that kind between the two.

remarks.para:
In space a grid's origin is a point of space, given by  and put onto the shape's plane;
, a point of the plane, is refused here. The shapes' own ToMesh members come
here.

member.param:
The shortest segment leaving  and landing on a triangle of the mesh, the one
 gives for the nearest triangle;
default when the method returns false.

member.remarks:

using (Tolerance.Use(new Tolerance(1E-1, 1E-1)))
{
    plate.CollidesWith(bolt);   // within a tenth, on this thread only
}

Scopes nest: each one disposed puts back the one it replaced. The scope belongs to the thread that
opened it — work handed to other threads, by Parallel or a task, sees the process-wide
setting, which is why the methods that spread their work, such as Clash3.Find, take the
tolerance as it stands when they are called and pass it on.
